<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Quadruple Alliance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1718">1718</a>–<a href="/years/1720">1720</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Quadruple Alliance (1718–1720) was fought by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, which under Philip V and his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-alberoni">Giulio Alberoni</a> had seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in defiance of the Utrecht settlement. The British fleet destroyed the Spanish navy off Cape Passaro in 1718 and French troops invaded northern Spain. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-hague-1720">Treaty of The Hague (1720)</a> Spain withdrew, and Austria exchanged Sardinia with Savoy for Sicily.</p></div>
